        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change extends `Owner.membershipLevel` in the established idiom of this class: a static derivation method that takes the relevant owner fields as parameters and returns the computed value. Adding `registrationDate` as a third parameter mirrors how sibling methods (`membershipNumber`, `ageBand`) already accept `LocalDate registrationDate`, so a maintainer would find it natural.\n\n- The tenure check is a single inline `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...) > 365` condition, consistent in weight with the existing `email`/`namesakeCount` increments \u2014 extracting a helper would be over-engineering, and no other method needs tenure, so there's nothing duplicated to factor out.\n- The logic stays in the right unit (membership-level derivation lives on `Owner` alongside the other derived values); the method isn't becoming a catch-all \u2014 it remains a focused, additive accumulate-then-cap computation.\n- The mapper's one-line delegation and both javadocs (method and `@link`) were updated to match the new signature and the 1\u20134 range, so the documentation stays coherent with the code."
      }
    ]
  }
}